## 6. Architecture

A diagram is at `docs/presentation/architecture.png`.

- Browser workspace: React and TypeScript, hash routing, a single persistent store, browser-local persistence with exit flush and visible storage failure, validated JSON backups at schema version 3.
- Deterministic core in `src/lib/`: curriculum constraints and diffs, teaching plans, evidence calculations (citation validator, fingerprints, Wilson intervals, coverage stages, report and brief), board payload normalisation and keyword filters, backup validation.
- Local API: Hono on Node 24. `/api/parse` for xlsx, csv, pdf, pptx and docx. `/api/collect/:provider/:board` for the two permitted job-board hosts, with board-token validation, a one-hour cache, a 15-second gap between fetches of the same board, at most 20 fetches per ten minutes, a 15 MB size cap, a 20-second timeout and plain error messages. `/api/agent` for optional model streaming with a deterministic fallback.
- Planned: a shared API and identity (plan W02) as the contract for Teams through Copilot Studio, Slack and LTI surfaces, so a university reaches Lyceum from the tools it already uses.

## 7. Data, sources and policies

- Source policies are shown in the app for each collection source: owner, method, retention, refresh, policy review date and a note on intended use. Greenhouse and Lever publish these APIs for employers' career pages; Lyceum fetches a named employer's board at low volume on request and does not collect from LinkedIn or anything behind a login. Scheduled or bulk collection would need confirmation of intended use first.
- Provenance per source: lecturer-supplied or collected, with provider, board, posting id, retrieval time and policy label. Publication dates are shown as published and never manufactured from the retrieval time.
- Everything is stored in the lecturer's browser. Backups may contain course material and uploaded learner records and belong to the lecturer. No data is sent to a provider unless a model key is configured, and then only the payload of the specific request.

## 8. Known limitations and not built

- No shared accounts, server permissions, server store or multi-device sync; the browser is the only persistence, with JSON backups as the recovery path.
- Collection covers two documented board APIs and manual paste. No page collectors for employer sites without an API, no snapshots of arbitrary sites, no cross-site vacancy clustering, no scheduled refresh.
- The Lever API does not state the employer name, so the site token is used.
- No comparable time windows yet, so no trend over time is reported.
- Assessment items are template-based; exact mark allocation, model answers and rubrics are pending.
- Slide packs are generated from saved data with no model-written text. Model-drafted slide content with lecturer review, selective regeneration, institutional templates, handouts, and DOCX or PDF export of the brief are pending.
- The Trends, Relevance Index, Acceptance test and Closed loop screens remain on synthetic fixtures and should be quarantined from the lecturer's navigation.
- The optional model integration uses an older SDK and a previous-generation model id; the intake route forces a tool call that current models reject. This is scheduled work.
- Accessibility: labels, focus, keyboard tabs, reflow and contrast are checked by the smokes; a full WCAG 2.2 AA audit with a screen reader is pending.
- No lecturer pilot has run; no educational or commercial validation is claimed.

## 9. Next steps

In order: quarantine the synthetic screens; the provider upgrade; comparable time windows for trends; employer naming for Lever; model-drafted slide content with lecturer review on top of the deterministic packs; DOCX and PDF export of the brief; code splitting; an accessibility pass; an OpenAPI description of collect, report and brief as the contract for the shared API; the shared API and identity when a pilot has a date; then the Teams or Slack surface for the pilot institution's tool.

## 10. Market and pitch references

Labelled estimates with sources are in the improvement plan, Sections 26 to 28: over 22,000 accredited institutions and over 14 million tertiary teachers worldwide (UNESCO); roughly 45,000 lecturers in Malaysia (MOHE 2023) across 20 public universities and about 355 private institutions (MIDA); adjacent curriculum software spend estimated between USD 0.48 billion and USD 3.5 billion for 2025 by publishers who disagree; incumbents Lightcast Skillabi and Chmura JobsEQ selling to institutions from above. The pitch follows the AWS five-V structure: Value, Visualize, Validate, Verify, Venture.

## 11. Repository map

- `docs/lyceum-improvement-plan.md`: the master plan with dated execution records.
- `DECISIONS.md`: the decisions log.
- `README.md`, `JUDGES.md`, `docs/lecturer-guide.md`: how to run, judge and use the prototype.
- `docs/presentation/`: pitch pack, deck brief, architecture diagram and app screenshots.
- `src/lib/evidence.ts`, `src/lib/collect.ts`, `server/collect.ts`: the research run's logic and collector.
- `src/lib/slides.ts`: the teaching pack and brief deck generator.
- `src/lib/curriculum.ts`, `src/lib/teachingPlan.ts`, `src/lib/workspaceBackup.ts`: curriculum, teaching and backup logic.
- `src/prove-*.ts` and `scripts/*-smoke.mjs`: the automated checks named in Section 5.
- `docs/history/`: the July 2026 implementation specification and as-built report, superseded by this document.
// What actually happened, step by step, told by role. Every event is derived
// from a record the workspace holds (a source, a quotation, a version, a brief),
// so the timeline can only show work that was really done.

import type { AppState } from "./store.ts";
import { SOURCE_POLICIES } from "../lib/collect.ts";
import { evidenceReport } from "../lib/evidence.ts";

export type RoleId = "folio" | "scout" | "atlas" | "quill" | "prism" | "lens" | "steward";
export interface Role { id: RoleId; name: string; job: string; reads: string; produces: string; cannot: string }
export const ROLES: Role[] = [
  { id: "folio", name: "Folio", job: "Course reader", reads: "Your syllabus, outline and uploaded documents", produces: "A course record with outcomes, topics and locators", cannot: "Declare a document official" },
  { id: "scout", name: "Scout", job: "Industry researcher", reads: "Permitted employer boards, on your request", produces: "Postings with link, publication date, retrieval time and text", cannot: "Collect without being asked, or change the curriculum" },
  { id: "atlas", name: "Atlas", job: "Curriculum mapper", reads: "The kept postings and the skills you name", produces: "Proposed exact quotations and skill-to-outcome mappings for you to confirm", cannot: "Confirm a quotation or a mapping for you" },
  { id: "quill", name: "Quill", job: "Course designer", reads: "The course brief, constraints and the evidence you confirmed", produces: "Outline revisions checked against hours, links and protected topics", cannot: "Approve its own revision" },
  { id: "prism", name: "Prism", job: "Teaching-material creator", reads: "A saved session and the evidence linked to its outcomes", produces: "An editable teaching pack with speaker notes", cannot: "Publish anything or write a word with a model" },
  { id: "lens", name: "Lens", job: "Evidence analyst", reads: "Reviewed postings and confirmed quotations", produces: "Counts with the denominator, intervals, coverage against targets", cannot: "Score employability or predict learning" },
  { id: "steward", name: "Steward", job: "Review assistant", reads: "The brief, its sources and the decision context", produces: "A brief with receipts, sent to the people who decide", cannot: "Decide; the lecturer and the university do" },
];

export interface RunEvent { at: string; role: RoleId; title: string; detail: string; tab?: AppState["studioTab"] }

const time = (iso: string) => iso;

export function runTimeline(state: AppState, subjectId: string | null): RunEvent[] {
  if (!subjectId) return [];
  const events: RunEvent[] = [];
  const name = (id: string) => state.people.find((p) => p.id === id)?.name ?? id;
  for (const draft of state.curriculumDrafts.filter((d) => d.subjectId === subjectId)) {
    for (const h of draft.history) {
      const titles: Record<string, string> = { created: "Revision started", saved: "Revision saved", checked: "Constraints checked", adopted: "Version adopted", discarded: "Revision discarded" };
      events.push({ at: h.at, role: "quill", title: titles[h.action] ?? h.action, detail: h.note + " (" + name(h.byPersonId) + ")", tab: h.action === "adopted" ? "history" : "curriculum" });
    }
  }
  const sources = state.evidenceSources.filter((s) => s.subjectId === subjectId);
  const batches = new Map<string, typeof sources>();
  for (const s of sources.filter((x) => x.collection)) {
    const key = s.collection!.label + "|" + s.collection!.retrievedAt;
    batches.set(key, [...(batches.get(key) ?? []), s]);
  }
  for (const [, batch] of batches) {
    const first = batch[0];
    const policy = SOURCE_POLICIES[first.collection!.provider];
    events.push({ at: first.addedAt, role: "scout", title: "Fetched on request, " + batch.length + " postings kept", detail: policy.name + " Â· retrieved " + time(first.collection!.retrievedAt) + " Â· " + batch.filter((b) => b.duplicateOf).length + " duplicate copies", tab: "evidence" });
  }
  for (const s of sources.filter((x) => !x.collection)) events.push({ at: s.addedAt, role: "folio", title: "Document recorded: " + s.title, detail: (s.organisation || "organisation not named") + " Â· pasted by " + name(s.addedBy), tab: "evidence" });
  const mentions = state.skillMentions.filter((m) => m.subjectId === subjectId);
  const byMinute = new Map<string, number>();
  for (const m of mentions) { const key = m.addedAt.slice(0, 16); byMinute.set(key, (byMinute.get(key) ?? 0) + 1); }
  for (const [minute, count] of byMinute) events.push({ at: minute + ":00.000Z", role: "atlas", title: count + " exact quotations confirmed", detail: "Each verified against its source text; paraphrases rejected", tab: "evidence" });
  const reviewed = sources.filter((s) => s.reviewed && !s.duplicateOf);
  if (reviewed.length) {
    const report = evidenceReport(subjectId, state.evidenceSources, state.skillMentions, state.skillMappings, state.clos.filter((c) => c.subjectId === subjectId));
    const latest = reviewed.map((s) => s.addedAt).sort().at(-1)!;
    const top = report.rows.filter((r) => r.postings > 0).slice(0, 3).map((r) => r.skill + " " + r.postings + " of " + report.eligible).join(", ");
    events.push({ at: latest, role: "lens", title: "Counted over " + report.eligible + " reviewed postings", detail: top ? "Top: " + top + ". Wilson 95% intervals shown; no score." : "No requirement quoted yet", tab: "evidence" });
  }
  for (const m of state.skillMappings.filter((x) => x.subjectId === subjectId)) {
    const labels = m.cloIds.map((id) => state.clos.find((c) => c.id === id)?.label ?? id).join(", ") || "no outcome";
    events.push({ at: m.updatedAt, role: "atlas", title: "Mapped " + m.skill + " to " + labels, detail: "Coverage " + m.stage + ", target " + m.target + (m.evidence ? " Â· " + m.evidence : ""), tab: "evidence" });
  }
  for (const s of state.teachingPlans.find((p) => p.subjectId === subjectId)?.sessions ?? []) events.push({ at: s.updatedAt, role: "prism", title: "Session saved: week " + s.week + ", " + s.topic, detail: s.minutes + " minutes Â· " + (s.cloIds.length ? "linked to " + s.cloIds.join(", ") : "no outcome linked") + " Â· teaching pack available", tab: "plan" });
  for (const t of state.testDrafts.filter((x) => x.subjectId === subjectId)) if (t.items.length) events.push({ at: state.subjectVersions.find((v) => v.id === t.courseVersionId)?.changedAt ?? "", role: "quill", title: t.items.length + " template assessment items drafted", detail: "Blueprint over " + t.blueprint.cloWeights.length + " outcomes Â· labelled as templates", tab: "assessment" });
  for (const b of state.evidenceBriefs.filter((x) => x.subjectId === subjectId)) {
    events.push({ at: b.createdAt, role: "steward", title: "Meeting brief prepared", detail: b.recommendation + " Â· by " + name(b.createdBy) + " Â· receipts attached", tab: "evidence" });
    if (b.sentAt) events.push({ at: b.sentAt, role: "steward", title: "Brief sent to " + b.recipients.map(name).join(", "), detail: "Read " + (state.notifications.filter((n) => n.briefId === b.id && n.read).length) + " of " + b.recipients.length + " so far", tab: "evidence" });
  }
  return events.filter((e) => e.at).sort((a, b) => a.at.localeCompare(b.at));
}
// Optional brand artwork: if public/brand/<name>.png exists (for example an
// illustration generated by the owner), show it; otherwise render the fallback
// so the page never shows a broken image.

import { useState, type ReactNode } from "react";

export function BrandImage({ name, alt, fallback, width, height, className }: { name: string; alt: string; fallback: ReactNode; width?: number | string; height?: number | string; className?: string }) {
  const [failed, setFailed] = useState(false);
  if (failed) return <>{fallback}</>;
  return <img src={"/brand/" + name + ".png"} alt={alt} width={width} height={height} className={className} loading="lazy" onError={() => setFailed(true)} style={{ maxWidth: "100%", height: "auto" }} />;
}
